WEBVTT

NOTE Paragraph boundaries measured from synthesis; timing within paragraphs is approximate.

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.367
Open-source intelligence turns
accessible information into an assessment

00:00:04.367 --> 00:00:08.234
relevant to a question. Collection
may include public technical records,

00:00:08.234 --> 00:00:12.317
published reports, service documentation,
and observable digital footprints.

00:00:12.317 --> 00:00:16.828
Threat intelligence connects such material
with information about adversary behavior

00:00:16.828 --> 00:00:20.051
and relevant threats. Models
can discover candidate sources,

00:00:20.051 --> 00:00:23.220
extract entities, and organize
material by source and date.

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:25.965
Relationship analysis needs
careful interpretation.

00:00:25.965 --> 00:00:29.355
Two domains using the same hosting
address may share a provider

00:00:29.355 --> 00:00:33.014
rather than an owner. Similar names
can refer to different entities,

00:00:33.014 --> 00:00:35.705
and infrastructure
relationships change over time.

00:00:35.705 --> 00:00:39.311
AI can propose connections and display
the supporting observations,

00:00:39.311 --> 00:00:42.701
but common infrastructure alone
does not establish attribution.

00:00:42.701 --> 00:00:47.060
Keep identity claims separate from the
technical relationships actually observed.

00:00:47.060 --> 00:00:50.388
Source evaluation also prevents
repeated claims from appearing

00:00:50.388 --> 00:00:54.200
stronger than they are. Several
reports may quote one original article.

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:56.615
Trace important claims
back to their origins,

00:00:56.615 --> 00:00:59.783
compare collection dates, and
examine conflicting accounts.

00:00:59.783 --> 00:01:03.862
Deceptive or incomplete material may
be coherent and professionally written.

00:01:03.862 --> 00:01:07.889
A useful analytical table records the
claim, original evidence, confidence,

00:01:07.889 --> 00:01:11.700
and competing explanation rather than
merely counting supporting links.

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:14.945
Structured analytic techniques
encourage explicit alternatives

00:01:14.945 --> 00:01:19.289
and examination of disconfirming evidence.
Models can organize competing hypotheses

00:01:19.289 --> 00:01:23.058
and flag contradictions, while analysts
judge relevance and credibility.

00:01:23.058 --> 00:01:26.774
The output should explain which
conclusions are supported, which remain

00:01:26.774 --> 00:01:30.438
uncertain, and what additional
collection could change the assessment.

00:01:30.438 --> 00:01:33.683
Building an OSINT workflow and
studying threat actor profiling

00:01:33.683 --> 00:01:36.980
develop these capabilities beyond
simple information gathering.
